# lib

This directory contains the converter's PlatformIO private libraries. Each
subdirectory owns one firmware component and is compiled into the application by
PlatformIO's Library Dependency Finder.

## Components

- `captive_portal_component`: Provides the first-boot/configuration web portal,
  DNS redirects, HTTP routes, form parsing, and NVS updates for device setup.
- `ems_bridge`: Defines the protocol-neutral bridge API between EMS/S2 concepts
  and the converter's internal sensor and actuator requests.
- `eth_wifi_component`: Initializes Ethernet and WiFi AP/STA networking,
  including captive-portal AP setup and route preference.
- `led_component`: Owns the device LED state model and maps firmware states to
  visible LED behavior.
- `modbus_component`: Handles low-level Modbus TCP/RTU communication with the
  configured appliance.
- `modbus_mapping_component`: Parses device templates and translates EMS/S2
  sensor and actuator requests into Modbus reads, writes, and sequences.
- `s2_library_wrapper`: Wraps the shared `s2-device-firmware` library so the
  converter can expose its appliance model and receive S2 callbacks.
- `shared_types`: Contains shared data structures, constants, queue messages,
  and appliance configuration types used across components.
- `storage_component`: Initializes and accesses persistent storage, including
  NVS configuration values and SPIFFS template storage.
- `time_module`: Provides time-related firmware helpers used by the converter.

## Development notes

Keep component-specific headers and implementation files inside the component
that owns the behavior. Shared structures belong in `shared_types`; generic
project-wide headers should only go in `include/` when they do not naturally fit
any component.

The intended dependency direction is:

- S2 protocol integration goes through `s2_library_wrapper`.
- Protocol-neutral EMS concepts go through `ems_bridge`.
- S2-to-Modbus decisions belong in `modbus_mapping_component`.
- Raw Modbus transport details belong in `modbus_component`.
